      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the first six prime numbers.\n2. Sum the first five prime numbers.\n3. Divide the sum by the sixth prime number.\n4. Find the remainder.\n\nThe first six prime numbers are: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13.\n\nStep 1: Sum the first five prime numbers.\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 + 7 + 11 = 28\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Divide the sum by the sixth prime number.\n\\[\n28 \\div 13\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Perform the division to find the quotient and the remainder.\n\\[\n28 \\div 13 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 2\n\\]\nThis means that 13 goes into 28 two times evenly, leaving a remainder of 2.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the first five primes is divided by the sixth prime is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
